{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "lesson": {
    "slug": "diag-data-ai-class-1",
    "subject": "data-ai",
    "title": "Computers, Data & AI Check-In: Where Am I?",
    "summary": "Explore step-by-step instructions, patterns, sorting, simple graphs and smart machines so we can see what you already know.",
    "age_band": "7-8",
    "difficulty": 1,
    "estimated_minutes": 60,
    "unit": "Week 1: Where am I?",
    "learning_objectives": [
      "Show I can follow and put instructions in order",
      "Show I can spot patterns and sort things",
      "Show what I know about computers, data and safe online habits"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "diagnostic",
      "week-1"
    ],
    "curriculum": {
      "course": "data-ai-class-1",
      "semester": 1,
      "week": 1
    }
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Welcome, Computer Explorer!"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "markdown": "Computers follow **instructions** exactly, one step at a time. A list of clear steps is called an **algorithm**. Today is a **check-in** to see what you already know. No computer is needed!"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "emoji": "🤖",
      "alt": "Beep boop!",
      "caption": "Beep boop!"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Stop 1: Instructions in order"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "markdown": "If you give a robot the steps for making a sandwich in the wrong order, you get a very silly sandwich! The **order** of steps matters."
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "question": {
        "type": "order",
        "prompt": "Put these steps for brushing teeth in order.",
        "items": [
          {
            "id": "a",
            "text": "Put toothpaste on the brush"
          },
          {
            "id": "b",
            "text": "Brush your teeth"
          },
          {
            "id": "c",
            "text": "Rinse your mouth"
          }
        ],
        "answer": [
          "a",
          "b",
          "c"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "explainer",
      "title": "A sandwich in the right order",
      "scenes": [
        {
          "caption": "First, put the bread on the plate.",
          "items": [
            {
              "emoji": "🍽️",
              "x": 50,
              "y": 75,
              "size": 3
            },
            {
              "emoji": "🍞",
              "x": 50,
              "y": 55,
              "id": "b1",
              "size": 3,
              "anim": "grow"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "caption": "Next, add the cheese.",
          "items": [
            {
              "emoji": "🍽️",
              "x": 50,
              "y": 75,
              "size": 3
            },
            {
              "emoji": "🍞",
              "x": 50,
              "y": 55,
              "id": "b1",
              "size": 3
            },
            {
              "emoji": "🧀",
              "x": 50,
              "y": 38,
              "id": "ch",
              "size": 2,
              "anim": "grow"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "caption": "Last, put the other bread on top. Now it is a sandwich! Order matters.",
          "items": [
            {
              "emoji": "🍽️",
              "x": 50,
              "y": 75,
              "size": 3
            },
            {
              "emoji": "🥪",
              "x": 50,
              "y": 52,
              "id": "b1",
              "size": 3,
              "anim": "bounce"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Stop 2: Patterns and sorting"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "markdown": "Computers love **patterns**. We can also **sort** things into groups, such as animals that fly and animals that swim."
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "question": {
        "type": "multiple_choice",
        "prompt": "Which one belongs in the group of fruits?",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "a",
            "text": "Banana"
          },
          {
            "id": "b",
            "text": "Chair"
          },
          {
            "id": "c",
            "text": "Pencil"
          }
        ],
        "answer": [
          "a"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "activity",
      "title": "Be the robot",
      "materials": [
        "a grown-up helper",
        "a small toy to hide"
      ],
      "instructions": [
        "Hide the toy in the room while your helper closes their eyes.",
        "Tell your helper the steps to find it, one at a time, such as walk forward 3 steps, turn left.",
        "Does your helper find the toy? If not, which step needs fixing?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Stop 3: Data and graphs"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "markdown": "**Data** is information we collect. We can count things with tally marks and draw a **pictogram** where each picture stands for one item."
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "question": {
        "type": "multiple_choice",
        "prompt": "A pictogram shows 3 🍎 for apples and 5 🍌 for bananas. Which fruit is more popular?",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "a",
            "text": "Apples"
          },
          {
            "id": "b",
            "text": "Bananas"
          }
        ],
        "answer": [
          "b"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Stop 4: Smart machines and staying safe"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "markdown": "Some machines can learn from examples. They are called **AI**, short for **artificial intelligence**. A phone that recognises your voice uses AI. But computers do not think or feel like people.\n\nOnline, keep your **password secret** and always ask a grown-up before you share anything or talk to someone."
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "question": {
        "type": "true_false",
        "prompt": "It is safe to tell strangers online your password.",
        "answer": [
          false
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "reveal",
      "prompt": "Can you think of a machine at home that follows instructions?",
      "answer_markdown": "A washing machine, microwave or toy robot all follow steps. They do not decide by themselves."
    },
    {
      "type": "brain_game",
      "game": "memory_match",
      "title": "Computer pairs",
      "goal": "Find the matching pairs.",
      "emojis": [
        "🤖",
        "💻",
        "📊",
        "🔢",
        "🔒",
        "🧩"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "summary",
      "points": [
        "An algorithm is a list of steps in order.",
        "A pattern repeats and helps us predict.",
        "Data can be counted and shown in a picture graph.",
        "AI is a machine that learns from examples, but it is not a person.",
        "Keep passwords secret and ask a grown-up first."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "style": "tip",
      "markdown": "Ready? Start the quiz. 12 questions, about 15 minutes. Have fun!"
    },
    {
      "type": "glossary",
      "terms": [
        {
          "term": "instructions",
          "meaning": "Clear steps that tell someone exactly what to do."
        },
        {
          "term": "algorithm",
          "meaning": "A list of steps to solve a problem, in the right order."
        },
        {
          "term": "pattern",
          "meaning": "Something that repeats again and again."
        },
        {
          "term": "sort",
          "meaning": "Put things into groups that are alike."
        },
        {
          "term": "data",
          "meaning": "Information we collect, like how many of each fruit."
        },
        {
          "term": "pictogram",
          "meaning": "A graph that uses little pictures to show numbers."
        },
        {
          "term": "artificial intelligence",
          "meaning": "A computer that learns from examples to do clever things."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
